  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "style": "AtlasKicker",
      "text": "SYNTHESIS ATLAS / RESEARCH EDITION 01"
    },
    {
      "style": "Title",
      "text": "Atlas invitation research across studies"
    },
    {
      "style": "Subtitle",
      "text": "A synthesis for research and product partners"
    },
    {
      "style": "AtlasSource",
      "text": "Prepared by Studio Templates / 30 September 2026 / Fictional teaching example"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Retest the v0.1 invitation route and role explanation before treating either as settled. Two fictional…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The synthesis separates observed task behavior from interview expectations. It gives a product partner…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Proposed decisions SY-D01 and SY-D02 request focused tests of navigation and role comprehension. SY-D03…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Caption",
      "text": "Read the study inventory before comparing results. Then follow the relationship matrix into the three…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Study inventory and overlap"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The unit of comparison is a study with a method, version and task. The table records those conditions…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "People are not study rows"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "S01 and S02 contain 13 study participations from 11 known distinct people. P02 and P06 recur. Eleven…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "S01 records first search, assistance and noticing confirmation. S02 records retrospective expectations…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Evidence relationships"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Read each row as a relationship to a synthesis claim. Support records the relevant observation;…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "S02 adds interview context, not another task-completion estimate. A blank outcome in one study is not a…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Synthesis claims and their limits"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "SY F01 Invitation access needs a version specific check"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Observation. In S01, six of eight first searched Members and four needed a hint. In S02, four of five…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Interpretation. The location under Settings may conflict with some first-time admins’ expectations. Two…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Proposed response SY-D01. Test a Members invitation entry against a feasible alternative while keeping…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "SY F02 Role questions need a comprehension check"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Observation. Three of eight in S01 raised role-scope questions: P02, P04 and P06. Three of five in S02…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Interpretation. The two methods expose related uncertainty, but a volunteered question and a prompted…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Proposed response SY-D02. Ask participants to apply the role description to a concrete permission…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "SY F03 Noticing is a narrow confirmation result"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Observation. All eight S01 participants noticed the confirmation, including the four who required…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Interpretation. Noticing a prototype state does not establish independent end-to-end completion, real…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Proposed response SY-D03. Preserve Atlas F03 and D03 as version-specific evidence. Request a task-based…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Applicability and next decisions"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "These are recommendations for a fictional review, not implementation commitments. The original Atlas…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "When to reopen the synthesis"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Review a claim when its product version, population, task wording, assistance rule or source access…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Missing records, quotations or identity mappings must remain explicit. Seek access through an…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Review trigger: when the proposed owners accept responsibility and the next protocol is agreed. Date:…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Source records"
    },
    {
      "style": "Caption",
      "text": "Each row resolves by ID to the accompanying synthesis_fixture.json, including the study inventory and…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Caption",
      "text": "Use this register with the study inventory. B records are interview notes; E records are the original…"
    }
